{
  "id": "zbrush",
  "name": "Maxon ZBrush",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "CAD / 3D",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "ZBrush.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.pixologic.zbrush"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://help.maxon.net/zbr/en-us/Content/html/user-guide/keyboard-shortcuts/shortcuts-by-category/shortcuts-by-category.html",
    "https://help.maxon.net/zbr/en-us/Content/html/user-guide/keyboard-shortcuts/keyboard-shortcuts.html",
    "https://docs.pixologic.com/user-guide/keyboard-shortcuts/shortcuts-by-category/"
  ],
  "note": "From the ZBrush user guide \"Shortcuts by Category\" page (the docs.pixologic.com pages now redirect to help.maxon.net/zbr). The page lists one set of keys and does not document separate Mac chords, so only `windows` is filled in. The section headings are used as context. Left out because the chord grammar cannot express them: every mouse and click-and-drag binding (the whole \"Edit mode Navigation\", \"Transpose\", \"Dynamesh\" and \"ZSpheres\" mouse sections, the Timeline key-frame mouse actions, \"Load selected item: Double-click on Lightbox thumbnail\", \"Assign custom hotkey Ctrl+Alt+click\", \"Move item to custom interface position Ctrl+Alt+drag\"); the hold-a-modifier bindings (\"Toggle ZAdd and ZSub: Alt\", \"Paint mask on object: Ctrl\", \"Reverse 2.5D brush effect: Alt\", \"Select Masking Brush: hold Ctrl while selecting\"); the \"~ + click\" / \"@ + click\" document-layer bindings; and \"Snapshot to Movie\", which is documented as Ctrl+Shift+! on US layouts and Shift+Ctrl+PageUp on UK layouts. The Transpose sub-headings \"Move mode - W\", \"Scale - E\" and \"Rotate - R\" repeat the Sculpting and Painting entries and are not listed twice. Multi-letter brush picks such as \"B - S - T\" are sequence actions.",
